# The binaries every Leap host takes from upstream rather than from a package, at these
# versions and these SHA-256s (docs/decisions.md § Every box has two ways in, § Leap hosts
# carry upstream's Compose). Read by a host's first boot (leap/firstboot.sh), which starts
# it on these, and by ansible/playbooks/server-update-leap.yml, which moves a running host
# to them and keeps the binary it replaced. Moving a pin is a commit here: the version and
# the release's own SHA-256 for both architectures, aarch64 for the Pis and x86_64 for the
# simulation (sim/microos/run-host.sh).
#
# The last two keys pin the Pi image every Leap host's card is written from, by its URL and
# openSUSE's SHA-256. plans/visit-runbook.md quotes the same pair, and no host reads them.
# .github/workflows/pi-image.yml inspects that image, and fails when the runbook quotes
# another SHA-256 or when a binary's SHA-256 here is not its release's.
#
# KEY=value lines only, no spaces and no quotes: a shell sources this file and a play
# splits each line at its "=".
